PROPERTY INSURANCE POLICY

This Property Insurance Policy (the "Policy") is entered into this 1st day of January, 2023, by and between ABC Insurance Company Ltd., a company incorporated under the laws of Ontario, Canada, with its head office located at 1234 Main Street, Toronto, Ontario, Canada ("ABC Insurance"), and John Doe, residing at 5678 Elm Street, London, NW1 2DT, UK ("Insured").

I. INSURANCE COVERAGE

A. Property Coverage

This Policy covers the Insured's residential property, a three-bedroom semi-detached house, located at 5678 Elm Street, London, NW1 2DT, UK ("Insured Property"). The Insured Property is insured for its actual cash value, determined as the replacement cost of the property less depreciation.

B. Perils Covered

The Insured Property is covered against the following perils:

1. Fire or lightning;
2. Explosion;
3. Riot or civil commotion;
4. Aircraft or articles dropped therefrom;
5. Vehicles or articles dropped therefrom;
6. Smoke from a heating system or from a building on fire;
7. Falling objects;
8. Weight of ice, snow, or sleet;
9. Water damage from ruptured pipes or from accidental overflow or discharge of water or steam from within a plumbing, heating, or air-conditioning system or from a household appliance;
10. Vandalism or malicious mischief;
11. Theft;
12. Volcanic eruption;
13. Windstorm or hail;
14. Damage caused by the collapse of a building or any part thereof.

